Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 08/27/2024]
1. Resonance energies from Ex in Endt 1998 and nuclear Q value. 
2. Er >= 624 keV: resonance strengths from Endt 1990, normalized to values listed in our table of standard strengths.
3. Er = 197 - 602 keV: measured resonance strengths from Iliadis et al. 1993 [already normalized to standard strengths].
4. Er = 308 keV: Gg = 1 eV is an approximate estimate.
5. Er = 161 keV: partial widths are estimated from measured wg_ag, C2S from (3He,d), and branching ratios reported in Ross et al. 1995.
6. Er = -1.4 keV: reduced width from (3He,d); Gg and Ga from Aboud et al. 2018.
7. Direct capture S factor is estimated using average experimental C2S values listed Endt 1990.
